%% (BUILT through the offer at P3 step 4a; only the AUDIO below is still missing)
sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    participant C as Customer
    participant TEL as Telephony
    participant IVR as IvrMachine
    participant PP as PromptPack
    participant PACK as DomainPack
    participant HOLD as HoldMachine
    participant ORCH as CallOrchestrator

    C->>TEL: dials +6621234000 (general hotline)
    TEL->>IVR: call arrives, ANI +66898887777
    IVR->>PACK: did("+6621234000")
    PACK-->>IVR: line unknown, skip_product_menu false

    IVR->>C: greeting.general, then notice.recording
    Note right of IVR: the recording notice is FIRST, on every<br/>call, whichever number was dialled

    Note over IVR,C: STEP 1 - which product line?
    IVR->>PP: lead-in + one option line each + reserved hint
    PP-->>IVR: pre-rendered clips, composed at call time (D80)
    IVR->>C: "กรุณาเลือกประเภทประกัน..." then "กด 1 ประกันรถยนต์", "กด 2 ประกันสุขภาพ", ...
    Note right of IVR: reordered if we recognise them, and RENUMBERED<br/>with the order — but it NEVER speaks their<br/>details aloud (D37). A menu cannot be one clip.
    C->>IVR: presses 2

    Note over IVR,C: STEP 2 - why are you calling?
    IVR->>C: "กด 1 แจ้งเข้ารักษาผู้ป่วยใน ... กด 4 สอบถามความคุ้มครอง ..."
    C->>IVR: presses 4

    IVR->>IVR: resolve each press through the presentation
    Note right of IVR: spoken key -> CANONICAL key (D81). With an<br/>option promoted these differ, so menu_path<br/>always holds ("2","4") whatever was pressed.
    PACK-->>IVR: line health, intent health.coverage.query
    IVR->>PACK: queue_for_intent - intent to skill to queue
    PACK-->>IVR: q_health_policy
    ORCH->>ORCH: enqueue(q_health_policy)

    Note over IVR,ORCH: ROUTING IS NOW SETTLED. No AI has run. (D37)<br/>Nothing below this line can change where the call goes.

    Note over HOLD,C: BUILT at P3 step 4a (D88). What is still missing is the AUDIO.
    HOLD->>C: "กรุณาถือสายรอสักครู่ค่ะ"
    Note right of HOLD: NO position and NO wait estimate (D91). There is no<br/>line to have a position in - the matcher re-solves the<br/>whole call x agent matrix every tick, so arrival order<br/>is not an input and a number would be a promise we break.
    HOLD->>C: "กด 1 เพื่อบันทึกข้อความ กด 2 เพื่อรอสายตามปกติ"

    alt presses 1
        C->>HOLD: 1
        HOLD->>ORCH: record_consent(recording + ai_processing), basis ivr_keypress_1
        Note right of ORCH: ONE keypress, BOTH scopes (D88). The prompt said<br/>exactly what would happen. health_data is separate<br/>and is still not asked for anywhere (Q24).
        ORCH->>ORCH: QUEUED -> INTAKE_ACTIVE
        HOLD->>C: "กรุณาเล่าเรื่อง... เมื่อเสร็จแล้วกด 1 อีกครั้ง"
        Note over HOLD,C: the driver RETURNS HERE. The recording outlives it,<br/>and is ended from outside by a VAD silence, the max<br/>duration, or an agent pressing Accept (D21, D88).
    else presses 2
        C->>HOLD: 2
        HOLD->>ORCH: record_consent(ai_processing, granted=FALSE)
        Note right of ORCH: the REFUSAL is recorded, not nothing. "They said no"<br/>and "we never asked" are different facts, and an empty<br/>consent list cannot tell you which happened (D88).
        HOLD->>C: "ได้ค่ะ กรุณาถือสายรอเจ้าหน้าที่"
    else says nothing
        HOLD->>C: "กรุณาถือสายรอสักครู่ค่ะ"
        Note right of HOLD: no re-prompt here, unlike the menu. The second<br/>chance is the re-offer at INTAKE_REOFFER_AFTER_S,<br/>and it is asked at most once more (D88).
    end

    Note over C,ORCH: every path proceeds, and the call is already correctly routed (D14).<br/>A wrong key is NEVER a strike (D82) - sorry, here are the options again.<br/>There is no operator key (D86): the way out is the menu's own "เรื่องอื่นๆ".
